 # SVG Texture
 
 ## What it is
-- **`UWidgetSVGTexture`** ("SVG Texture", `NameTBD/Widgets/WidgetSVGTexture.h`): a `UObject` asset made by importing a `.svg`, that **owns a `UTexture2D` subobject** (`Texture`, the SVG as drawn, cooked with the asset) and implements **`ISlateTextureAtlasInterface`** (`GetSlateAtlasData`: the whole texture), as a Paper2D sprite does. So it is picked as a Brush's Image (Brush Resource allows Texture, Material and Slate Texture Atlas Interface) on an Image, a Border, a button style...: import the SVG, set it on the brush. Blueprint: `Set Brush From Atlas Interface`, or **`GetTexture`** for anything that wants a Texture 2D.
-- **Why not a `UTexture2D` subclass** (v1): `UTexture2D` is `MinimalAPI`; most of its virtuals are not exported, so a plugin subclass fails to link (LNK2001 on `Serialize`, `PostLoad`, `CreateResource`...). Only exported calls are made on the owned texture (`Source`, `PreEditChange` / `PostEditChange`, settings).
-- **Fidelity:** drawn (editor only) into the texture's source pixels at **Resolution Scale** (default 4) x the SVG's own size (width/height, else viewBox), the longest side held to **Max Resolution** (default 2048). The texture is made with UI settings: `TC_EditorIcon` (uncompressed RGBA), sRGB, `TEXTUREGROUP_UI`, Never Stream, **mips (`TMGS_SimpleAverage`)** - so it is sharp at and below Resolution Scale x its size and filters cleanly when drawn smaller. The brush's Image Size on drop is the texture's size (Resolution Scale x the SVG size), as for any texture.
-- **Colours (the "black SVG" fix):** **Colors** (`TArray<FWidgetSVGColor>`, `EditFixedSize`) lists every colour the SVG uses (fills, strokes, gradient stops; first-use order; opacity left out) with **Draw As** next to it, edited inline in the asset's Details (double-click: the generic asset editor). Draw As alpha multiplies the SVG's own opacity. **Draw In White (Tint With Brush)** (`bDrawInWhite`, default off) draws every colour white keeping opacity, so the Brush Tint / Color and Opacity colours it. A shape with no fill is black in SVG: that is the black entry.
-- **Redraw:** editing Resolution Scale, Max Resolution, Draw In White or Colors redraws from `SVGSource` (the file's text, kept in the asset) and rebuilds the texture (`PreEditChange(nullptr)` waits for a running build, `Source.Init`, `PostEditChange`); not while a picker/spin box is dragged (`Interactive` changes are skipped). Undo redraws from the restored settings. Reimport reads the file again, keeping each still-present colour's Draw As.
-- Editor-only data: `SVGSource`, `Colors`, the settings, `SVGSize`, `AssetImportData`. A cooked game has the asset and its texture.
+- **An SVG Texture is an ordinary `UTexture2D`** made by importing a `.svg`, so every texture picker (a Brush's Image), `Set Brush From Texture`, Image Size on drop and thumbnails work as for any image. The SVG and its settings ride on it as Asset User Data: **`UWidgetSVGTextureData`** (`UAssetUserData`, `NameTBD/Widgets/WidgetSVGTexture.h`, editor-only: `IsEditorOnly` strips it when cooking, so a game has only the texture).
+- **Earlier designs, and why not:**
+  - v1, a `UTexture2D` subclass: `UTexture2D` is `MinimalAPI` and most of its virtuals aren't exported, so a plugin subclass fails to link (LNK2001 on `Serialize`, `PostLoad`, `CreateResource`...).
+  - fix1, a `UObject` owning a texture behind `ISlateTextureAtlasInterface`: the Brush's Image picker didn't list it.
+  - Only exported or virtual calls are made on textures: member settings, `Source.Init` / `UseHashAsGuid`, `PreEditChange` / `PostEditChange` (all linked in fix1), and `IInterface_AssetUserData` (`AddAssetUserData`, `GetAssetUserDataOfClass`) through the interface.
+- **Fidelity:** drawn (editor only) into the texture's source pixels at **Resolution Scale** (default 4) x the SVG's own size (width/height, else viewBox), the longest side held to **Max Resolution** (default 2048). `ApplyTextureSettings` sets the texture up on import: `TC_EditorIcon` (uncompressed RGBA), sRGB, `TEXTUREGROUP_UI`, Never Stream, **mips (`TMGS_SimpleAverage`)**. So it is sharp at and below Resolution Scale x its size and filters cleanly when drawn smaller. Image Size on drop is the texture's size (Resolution Scale x the SVG size).
+- **Colours (the "black SVG" fix):**
+  - **Colors** (`TArray<FWidgetSVGColor>`, `EditFixedSize`) lists every colour the SVG uses (fills, strokes, gradient stops; first-use order; opacity left out), with **Draw As** next to each. Draw As alpha multiplies the SVG's own opacity.
+  - **Draw In White (Tint With Brush)** (`bDrawInWhite`, default off) draws every colour white keeping opacity, so the Brush Tint / Color and Opacity colours it. A shape with no fill is black in SVG: that is the black entry.
