 ## Pieces
-- **Rasterizer:** nanosvg, vendored header-only in `Source/ThirdParty/nanosvg` (upstream commit and licence in its README), on `NameTBD`'s private include path. Compiled only in `WidgetSVGTexture.cpp` under `WITH_EDITOR`, as C++ inside `namespace NameTBDNanoSVG` (`NANOSVG_CPLUSPLUS` / `NANOSVGRAST_CPLUSPLUS`; the C headers it uses are included first, outside the namespace), so it never clashes with the engine's own copy. Output is straight (not premultiplied) RGBA with edge colours spread into clear pixels; swapped to BGRA for `Source.Init(..., TSF_BGRA8)` + `UseHashAsGuid`.
+- **Rasterizer:** nanosvg, vendored header-only in `Source/ThirdParty/nanosvg` (upstream commit and licence in its README), on `NameTBD`'s private include path.
+  - Compiled only in `WidgetSVGTexture.cpp` under `WITH_EDITOR`, as C++ inside `namespace NameTBDNanoSVG` (`NANOSVG_CPLUSPLUS` / `NANOSVGRAST_CPLUSPLUS`; the C headers it uses are included first, outside the namespace), so it never clashes with the engine's own copy.
+  - Output is straight (not premultiplied) RGBA with edge colours spread into clear pixels; swapped to BGRA for `Source.Init(..., TSF_BGRA8)` + `UseHashAsGuid`.
 - **Recolouring** edits the parsed `NSVGshape` paints (`0xAABBGGRR`) before rasterizing; `RasterizeSVG` also refreshes `Colors` (only assigned when it differs).
-- **Editor** (`NameTBDEditor/Private/WidgetSVGTextureFactory.*`): `UWidgetSVGTextureFactory` (text factory, `svg`, priority `DefaultImportPriority + 10`, also the `FReimportHandler`); `FWidgetSVGTextureAssetTypeActions` (User Interface category, imported asset so Reimport / source file show); `UWidgetSVGThumbnailRenderer` (the texture fitted on a dark tile). Registered in `FNameTBDEditorModule::StartupModule`. Colours in `NameTBDColors.h` (`Colors::SVGTexture`).
+- **Editor** (`NameTBDEditor/Private/WidgetSVGTextureFactory.*`):
+  - `UWidgetSVGTextureFactory`: text factory for `svg`, priority `DefaultImportPriority + 10`. It makes the `UTexture2D`, adds the data, and draws. It is also the `FReimportHandler`, for textures carrying the data, at a priority above the engine's texture reimporter.
+  - `FWidgetSVGTextureDetails`: registered and unregistered in `NameTBDEditor.cpp`.
 
 ## Checked outside the engine
 - nanosvg in the namespace compiles with g++ and links beside a plain C copy (no duplicate symbols); an SVG path with no fill parses as `0xFF000000` and draws white after recolouring; gradient stops are reached and recoloured.
 
 ## Still open
 - **SVG features nanosvg lacks:** `<text>`, filters, masks, clip paths, `<use>`/symbols, most CSS (`<style>` beyond simple cases), images. Such parts are dropped. A file that relies on them needs flattening (e.g. text to paths) before import.
-- **Image Size on drop** is the texture size, not the SVG size. Reporting the SVG size (overriding `GetSurfaceWidth/Height`) was left out: the engine also uses those for drawing.
+- **Image Size on drop** is the texture size (Resolution Scale x the SVG size), not the SVG size: a plain Texture 2D can't report another size. Set Image Size by hand, or Resolution Scale 1 for an exact match (and less sharpness).
 - Sharp beyond Resolution Scale x the size needs a higher scale (more memory) - there is no runtime re-draw at the widget's size.
 
 ## Unverified (no engine here)
-- That it compiles and links against 5.7: `FSlateAtlasData`'s constructor (texture, start UV, size UV as `FVector2D`), `FTextureSource::Init` / `UseHashAsGuid` signatures, `IsImportedAsset` / `GetResolvedSourceFilePaths` on `FAssetTypeActions_Base`.
-- That the Brush's Image picker offers SVG Textures (it lists Slate Texture Atlas Interface assets, as for Paper2D sprites) and that the designer sets Image Size from the texture.
-- That non-power-of-two sizes get mips in 5.7 (if not, a non-square or non-power-of-two SVG Texture has none and is less clean when drawn smaller).
-- That editing Colors in the asset's Details updates widgets using it at once, and that the factory wins `.svg` over Interchange / Epic's SVG Importer when those are on.
+- That it compiles against 5.7: `UTexture::AssetImportData` being reachable, `IInterface_AssetUserData` on `UTexture`, `AddExternalObjectProperty`, and `UAssetUserData` being subclassable from a plugin.
+- That a class layout on `Texture2D` is applied alongside the engine's `Texture` one (details customizations apply per class in the hierarchy), and that nothing else in the engine registers `Texture2D`.
+- That non-power-of-two sizes get mips in 5.7 (if not, such SVG Textures have none and are less clean when drawn smaller).
+- That the factory wins `.svg` over Interchange / Epic's SVG Importer when those are on.
